<div style="background-color: #e0f2f7; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px; text-align: center;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin-bottom: 10px;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Our Traditional Style of Dress – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 25%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 75%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 4th Grade (CEFR: A1.2)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Our Traditional Style of Dress</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Let's Dress for a Dance.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Edit classmates' written work.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write simple descriptions about traditional clothing (e.g., 'The pollera is beautiful.'). Can edit, for clarity, classmates' sentences about traditional dress (e.g., add 'colorful' to describe the dress). Can revise, for detail, written descriptions of traditional clothing (e.g., add 'worn' at festivals to describe the dress).</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333; background-color: #f0f8ff;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 40%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 10%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><i>(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</i></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher shows pictures of different traditional Panamanian clothing (e.g., a pollera, a montuno). Students quickly write down 1-2 words that describe each piece of attire on small sticky notes. For example, for 'pollera', they might write 'beautiful' or 'dress'. This activates prior vocabulary and connects to the theme "Let's Dress for a Dance." and the scenario "Our Traditional Style of Dress".</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher writes a simple sentence on the board about one of the clothes, for example: "The pollera is pretty." Then, the teacher models how to make it more descriptive by adding adjectives, like "The pollera is a very beautiful dress." The teacher clearly pronounces the /w/ sound in 'wearing' while demonstrating an example sentence "She is wearing a beautiful pollera." The teacher also models sounding out words like /dr/ /ɛs/ for 'dress' to reinforce the link between sounds and spelling for writing.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is 'pretty' a description word?" (Expected answer: Yes!)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Can we add more words to make our sentence better?" (Expected answer: Yes!)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><i>(Input of new language/content)</i></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short, illustrated narrative excerpt (a few sentences) describing traditional Panamanian clothing and its use for events. For example:</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0; font-style: italic;">"Women in Panama wear the pollera for special celebrations. It is very beautiful and has colorful embroidery. Men often wear a montuno, which is traditional clothing for festive events. They showcase their cultural attire during a dance. Children admire the pretty jewelry too."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Describing traditional clothing using present simple and present continuous, and explaining its cultural significance.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> The teacher reads the text aloud. Students read along silently. Then, they answer simple questions to check understanding of key details related to traditional dress and events.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question:</b> "What is the story about?" (Expected answer: Traditional Panamanian clothes/dresses.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> "The pollera is old-fashioned." (False. It is beautiful, worn for celebrations). "Men wear the montuno for festive events." (True)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching:</b> Match pictures of pollera/montuno with a sentence like "This is beautiful attire."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">8-10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><i>(Accuracy focus on Writing)</i></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice writing simple descriptive sentences using the present continuous ("She is wearing...") and present simple ("Women wear this dress at festivals.") with target vocabulary (attire, beautiful, cultural, festive, pretty, traditional clothing, jewelry, celebration, event, wear, represent).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 1 (Controlled Practice - Cloze sentences):</b> The teacher provides sentences about traditional clothing with blanks. Students fill in the blanks with appropriate vocabulary words from a word bank (e.g., 'beautiful', 'festive', 'wear', 'jewelry', 'celebration').<br>Example: "The pollera is a _____ dress. Women _____ it for a _____. They also use _____." (Possible answers: beautiful, wear, celebration, jewelry).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 2 (Semi-controlled - Sentence Expansion):</b> The teacher gives a basic sentence, and students expand it by adding adjectives or phrases. For instance, start with "She is wearing a dress." Students revise it to "She is wearing a beautiful, colorful dress for a dance." or "She is wearing a traditional dress at a festival." This targets the learning outcome of adding detail.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 3 (Pair Writing & Peer Check):</b> Students work in pairs. Each student chooses a picture of traditional attire and writes two simple sentences to describe it (e.g., "She is wearing a pollera. It is pretty."). They then exchange their sentences with their partner. The partner reads the sentences and, using a simple checklist (e.g., "Does it describe the picture? Is it a complete sentence?"), provides feedback for clarity. This introduces the concept of peer editing.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">12-15 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><i>(Communicative task)</i></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task format:</b> Collaborative writing and peer editing/revision.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students will work in pairs. Each student selects a different image of a person wearing traditional Panamanian clothing (e.g., different types of polleras, a montuno). Individually, they write a short paragraph (3-4 sentences) describing the attire, focusing on what the person is wearing (Present Continuous), what the clothing represents, and when it is worn (Present Simple). They should use vocabulary like 'attire', 'beautiful', 'cultural', 'festive', 'celebration', 'event', 'wear', 'represent', 'showcase'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Once written, students exchange their paragraphs with their partner. Each partner then acts as an editor and revises the other's work based on the learning outcomes:
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Editing for clarity:</b> Add adjectives (e.g., 'colorful', 'pretty') to make descriptions clearer.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Revising for detail:</b> Add information about where or when the clothing is 'worn' (e.g., 'worn at festivals', 'worn during a dance').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Checking for correct use of Present Continuous and Present Simple.</li>
                </ul>
                Students write their suggestions directly on the partner's paper using a different colored pen or pencil. Then they return the papers and discuss the suggestions, making final revisions to their own descriptions.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10-12 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><i>(Formative assessment)</i></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative assessment strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist and peer assessment based on a simple rubric.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students submit their final, revised written descriptions of traditional clothing along with the initial draft and their partner's editing suggestions. The teacher collects these to assess their ability to write descriptions and effectively edit/revise.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity:</b> Are the descriptions clear and easy to understand?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of Target Vocabulary:</b> Does the writing include words like 'attire', 'beautiful', 'cultural', 'festive', 'wear', 'celebration', 'event', 'jewelry'?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar:</b> Correct use of Present Continuous and Present Simple.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Editing/Revision:</b> Were appropriate suggestions made by the partner? Were the revisions incorporated effectively by the writer to add clarity and detail? (e.g., adding 'colorful' or 'worn at festivals').</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer the following questions on a small slip of paper:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one new thing you learned about writing descriptions today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Was it easy or difficult to help your partner edit their work? Why?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">6-8 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of editing your partner's writing did you find most helpful for your own writing?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can we make our sentences even more interesting next time we write about traditional clothing?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this lesson to help students write and edit their descriptions? (e.g., specific activities, models, peer interaction). The peer editing was effective in achieving the objective, and students engaged well with adding details.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for the next lesson (Lesson 5: Mediation & Integration)? Some students struggled with consistently using the Present Continuous vs. Present Simple. For the next lesson, I will provide more guided practice in distinguishing these tenses and ensure clear sentence starters are available for the project. I also need to reinforce phonemic awareness like /t/ in 'these' during dictation for the final task.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In Lesson 5, students will integrate their knowledge of traditional clothing by creating a visual presentation (21st Century Skills Project) and mediating information about different traditional garments for others, incorporating the writing and editing skills they practiced today.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">4-5 min</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>